# Fatehold Charm's second mode: "Return target spell or creature to its owner's hand." Bot2's Mox Sapphire is a permanent but
# not a creature, so it is no candidate; Bot2's Llanowar Elves is, and goes back to Bot2's hand. Nothing is drawn and no Jace
# token is made: only the mode chosen happens (CR 700.2).

[Bot1 Deck]
Tundra
Mox Sapphire
Fatehold Charm
Island x4
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Mox Sapphire
Forest x4
Forest x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Tundra.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Tundra.Activate(Ability: {W})
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Fatehold Charm.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Return target spell or creature)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire)
Bot1.Target(Llanowar Elves)
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Hand.Count = 6
Bot2.Hand = Llanowar Elves; Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Mox Sapphire
Bot1.Hand.Count = 5
Bot1.Graveyard = Fatehold Charm
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 2
